/**
 * The set of Wikipedia titles /wiki/[slug] will render, as a compile-time
 * constant. Generated from the Wikimedia pageviews API: the top 1,000 articles
 * per day over 90 days, deduplicated, with namespaced titles and Main_Page
 * removed, lowercased.
 *
 * Why this exists: /wiki/[slug] is the only expensive route on the site, and
 * essentially all of its traffic is automated. Measured over one day: 98.28K
 * function invocations against 101.92K edge requests — a ~1:1 ratio, meaning
 * clients that fetch the HTML and none of the page assets, which is not what a
 * browser does. Adding `Disallow: /wiki/` to robots.txt moved that number by
 * about 9%, so whatever is responsible ignores robots.txt, and almost certainly
 * sends a browser user-agent too — which is why user-agent filtering was not
 * the answer either.
 *
 * A crawler enumerating Wikipedia's ~7M title space misses this list almost
 * every time; a reader looking something up hits it almost every time. That
 * asymmetry is the whole idea. Unknown titles are rejected before any Wikipedia
 * fetch, sanitize, parse or render happens, so a rejected request costs one
 * invocation and essentially nothing else — and invocations were only $0.06 of
 * the $0.90/day. The other $0.84 was the work this check skips.
 *
 * Keys are lowercased deliberately. Wikipedia titles are case-sensitive beyond
 * the first letter, so lowercasing can only admit a request that would
 * otherwise be rejected; it cannot reject a valid one.
 *
 * The cost of the gate is coverage: an article outside this set now 404s. To
 * widen it, regenerate over a longer window. To remove the gate entirely, drop
 * the isRenderableTitle() calls in app/wiki/[slug]/page.tsx — nothing else
 * depends on this file.
 *
 * Generated 2026-08-19 — 14232 titles.
 */
